================================================================================
NOT reused: Forge Mod Loader (FML) / FancyModLoader (LGPL)
================================================================================
The kernel's Forge/NeoForge compatibility is an independent clean-room
implementation written from public formats and runtime contracts (the mods.toml
schema, JarInJar metadata, the IEventBus/registry API contracts, the Maven
version-range grammar, Mixin). It contains NO source from FML or FancyModLoader
(GNU LGPL v2.1+), which were consulted only as behavioural references.

The genuine Forge / NeoForge universal jars are NEVER bundled — they are
runtime-supplied (compileOnly linkage only) and act solely as passive ABI
carriers. No FML/FancyModLoader lifecycle is booted or reflectively driven.
